WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome back to the show
in person.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.267
-Thank you! I know!

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.701
-I mean...
-We're back.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.467
-You're back in New York City.
-Here we are.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.234
-This is your hometown.
-This is it.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.701
-How's it feel?
-Feels great.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.634
-It does, right?
-It feels amazing.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.767
-I wanted to ask you because
tonight's a big show for us.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.200
We have -- obviously, you're on.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.801
But I mean, we have, the Olympic
opening ceremonies was tonight

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:23.133
and I heard that you were almost
in an Olympic commercial once.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.300
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.834
-Is that true?
-Yes.

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:28.834
Well, I was in
an Olympic commercial.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.834
-You were?
-I don't think it aired.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.167
Because I might -- I --

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.801
[ Laughs ]
Okay, so here's the story.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.801
The story is I went in
to audition

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.267
and you know, when you first
start auditioning,

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:42.300
I went in as a dancer
and kind of like whatever.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.100
And they were like,
"Okay, can you dance?"

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.467
I danced and then I talked
and I read the copy

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.968
and I did the things,
and then they were like,

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.200
"By the way" -- I'm walking out
and I'm like, I nailed this.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.567
I killed this.
-I got this.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.667
-I got this.
I was great today.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.367
Today was my day.
-Yes, exactly.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:59.067
-I'm walking out and I'm like,
"Okay, bye, thank you.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.234
Thank you so much. Thank you."
And I walk out

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.467
and the guy says to me,
right before I leave, he goes,

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.968
"Hey, by the way,
can you do trampoline?"

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.067
And I go, "Yeah."

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.567
And I walk out,
thinking nothing of it.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:11.767
-Sure. Yeah.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.200
-Can I do a trampoline?
Are you kidding me?

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.634
-I get there and I do
all the things, I dance, I sing,

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:18.567
and then they bring out this
trampoline and they're like,

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.801
"Okay!"
-"Let's see what you got."

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.200
-"Do it!"

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.667
And I was like...okay.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.534
They're like, "You know, you do
the flips and the things."

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:31.000
And I was like, "Sure,
I'll do the trampoline."

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.834
I get up there and I'm like...

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.801
That was it.
That's all I had.

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:40.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.501
-Cut to c--
Is that all she does?

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:43.734
Did she do the trampoline?
-I did this!

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.901
I did this, I jumped,
and I did some of this.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.634
-You posed.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.167
-It was awful.
-That's not doing trampoline.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.567
-And they were like, "You said
you could do trampoline."

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.801
And I said, "No, I..."
-I'm sorry.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:56.734
-I did, but I didn't know
what you meant.

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.300
-How's the fam?

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.834
-Everybody's good.
-Two teenagers.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.501
-I know.
-Wow, is that wild.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:04.601
-I know, does anybody else
have teenagers right now?

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:06.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Laughs ]

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.767
-It's interesting, right?
-It is. It is.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.567
You know, they go from like
being these babies,

00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.868
and then when they turn
like 11 1/2, 12,

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:15.701
they become like adult people
in a little body.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.300
-I know, I know.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.133
I'm like -- every second,
I love hanging out with my kids

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.801
because I just don't want you
to grow up, but I do.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.334
-What they do is
that they need to, like,

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:27.100
distance themselves a little.
You know, it's my life.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.968
I have my own identity.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:31.167
I am who I am, this is what
I feel about the world.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:33.434
This is what I think.
And, you know, it's like,

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:34.767
Oh, my God, and I'm like,

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.434
"Baby, you want to sit
on my lap?"

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:37.601
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.767
-No, I don't now.
I'm a teenager. Not at all.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.834
-Mom, stop. Stop touching me.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.367
-I'll tell you
who is here tonight --

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.534
your mom is here.

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:46.534
-Who also likes me
to still sit on her lap.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.200
-Lupe is here tonight.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.200
-Hi, Mom.
-Hi, beautiful.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.367
Oh, my god, she is
the prettiest, the coolest.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:58.200
Is that --

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.334
Is that where you get
your drive? Is that --

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.467
-From my mom?
-Yeah.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:02.801
-Where do you think?
-I think I get my --

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:06.067
like, my personality
from my mom, a little bit.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.901
And you know, both my mom
and dad worked really hard.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:11.133
-Yeah.
-So I definitely --

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.834
-I don't know anyone
that works as hard as you.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.334
-I know. I don't know
what's wrong with me.

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.467
I'm not well.
-No, you are unbelievable.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.000
But I've known you
since "Saturday Night Live,"

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.734
but I've seen in every --
-I know.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.133
-Every aspect,
and you're just there

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.968
and you're just mentally
in the game and you're like,

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.400
"Yeah, cool. What's up?
We'll do that," blah blah.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.934
-What's next? Let's do it!
-"We'll do this. What's next?"

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.267
-I go...
-This is fun!

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:29.434
-But like, "Marry Me."

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.934
You go, "Great,
I'm in this movie."

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:32.601
That's enough for me.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:33.901
-I mean, I grew up in the Bronx.

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.601
My mom'll tell you,
we grew up in the Bronx.

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:37.267
We really didn't have a lot.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:39.234
You know,
this is a dream come true.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.400
Everything I do,
every single day,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.334
I feel so incredibly blessed.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.534
I feel so lucky to be doing
what I'm doing.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.501
I always wanted to sing.
I always wanted to dance.

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.534
My mother loved musicals,
you know,

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.300
she showed me them from
when I was very, very little,

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.601
and I just had all these dreams
of like doing that.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.934
And so now I'm doing it.
So why not do it all the time?

00:03:57.934 --> 00:04:00.200
I'll do it all the time.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.033
You got it. Everybody knows.
-Yeah, yeah. But I mean...

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.834
-You guys -- The Roots want
to play all the time.

00:04:05.834 --> 00:04:07.434
-Yeah.
-All they want to do is play.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.100
Every chance you get
to pick up a guitar,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.801
whether you're playing or not,
whether you're at work,

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.567
you're doing what you love.
-You just want to do, like...

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:14.801
Just play.
-Yeah. You know that.

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:17.467
-I know, but you also did
the soundtrack to this.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.667
-I did.

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:21.000
-You and Maluma are all over --
this is all you.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.467
And this is out now.

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.000
The movie comes out next week.
-Yes! Look at it!

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.501
Yay!
-Ah, there you go!

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:29.834
-It never gets old for me.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:32.067
Yes, this was actually
the first time

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.234
since I did the movie "Selena"
where I actually got to --

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:35.601
I didn't sing
in the movie "Selena."

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.267
That was Selena's voice.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.634
-So this is the first time
I got to, like, sing,

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.834
make an album for a film.

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:43.968
It is like joining
my two worlds together.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.300
I also got to play a character

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.868
who was, you know,
a lot like myself.

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:50.367
You know,
she's in the spotlight,

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:54.667
personal life, public life,
trying to make it all work.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.100
You know,
failing miserably at times.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.901
You know what I mean?
Doing all the things.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.400
But it's a really,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.701
really great kind of look
behind the behind the scenes.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.033
-Yeah, I remember the last time

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:08.133
you were here with Maluma.
-Yes.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:09.801
-You actually had a scene
in the movie

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.167
where you're supposed
to be at a concert.

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:13.000
You guys are doing your famous
duet in character.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.167
-Yeah.

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.801
-And instead of re-creating
a fake concert

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:19.300
on a movie set somewhere,
you crashed Maluma's --

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.300
-Oh, I did. We did.
-...Maluma's concert.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.534
-Yes, he was having like two
nights at Madison Square Garden.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:27.801
And of course,
the producer in me is like,

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:29.567
"We can take advantage of that."
-[ Laughing ] Yeah, yeah.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.133
It's like, yeah.
Alright, he's already got --

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.934
-We have a scene, a big scene
in an arena.

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.434
Why don't we do it
at your concert?

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.367
And he was like, "Okay..."
-Yeah.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:40.834
-How'd that feel?
People must have went bonkers --

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.167
-It was amazing.
-...when you walked out.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.834
-It was amazing, yeah.
I came up out of the floor

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.667
dressed like the character
in the movie,

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.100
and this scene is in the movie.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.267
And they just didn't expect me
to come out at his concert.

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.300
I've never been out
at one of his concerts.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.133
And the crowd went wild,

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:56.934
and we got it all on film
and we sang together.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.534
And it was -- it was awesome.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.100
-And I will say the whole --

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:01.968
you're on the whole soundtrack,
is you and Maluma.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:04.300
I mean, this thing is --
it's awesome.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.868
-Yeah, it's not like
a Jennifer Lopez J.Lo album

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:09.834
or even a Maluma album.
It's a Kat and Bastian album.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:13.534
These are songs that I really
picked for the characters

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:15.801
and that really kind of like
further along the story,

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:17.634
just like any good musical.
-Yeah.

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:19.334
-And it really tells
the love story,

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:22.234
the journey of, you know,
kind of finding your true love.

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:24.300
-We're here with Jennifer Lopez!

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:30.667
Her new movie "Marry Me"
is in theaters February 11th.

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:34.167
And I should mention that I have
a cameo in this movie.

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:35.300
-You do have a cameo.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.000
-We're in a movie together.
-Two cameos.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.667
-I know. I had two cam--
Pretty important scenes.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:39.968
-Really important scenes.

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:41.801
Actually, one of the scenes
was really important.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.067
It was very emotional.

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:44.634
Because it's one
of those moments

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.667
where, like,
people don't get to see

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:50.167
where I kind of had to, like,
let down my guard, too,

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:54.567
where she suffers this terrible
kind of public humiliation

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.100
and is on her way home.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:00.934
And like the night talk show
hosts do, they're roasting her.

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:05.000
And she's crying on the floor
in a puddle.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.801
You know what I mean?

00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:07.300
And it's just, like,
one of those moments

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.067
that people don't
really think about.

00:07:09.067 --> 00:07:10.534
You know, you don't think,
"Oh, God.

00:07:10.534 --> 00:07:13.400
Maybe they're laughing at home.
Maybe they can take a joke."

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:14.834
And sometimes it just --
-It just hurts.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.000
-It just hurts.
-It just hurts, yeah.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.601
And this was the first time,
like, I got to, like, do that.

00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:21.300
Because, you know,
we're in show business.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.834
We like to
put our best foot forward.

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:25.501
We're out here. You don't need
to know about our nonsense.

00:07:25.501 --> 00:07:28.200
You just sing the song,
do the dance.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.033
We entertain.
We have a good time.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.634
But there's a human being there,

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.634
and I think this movie
kind of gets into that.

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:36.267
And you are the talk show host
who's roasting me.

00:07:36.267 --> 00:07:37.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.734 --> 00:07:40.434
-I love that I got permission
to roast your character, yeah.

00:07:40.434 --> 00:07:42.167
But I do think you are perfect
for that

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:43.300
'cause you get to see
all the stuff.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.968
And it's such public stuff.

00:07:44.968 --> 00:07:47.534
Everything you do is so public,
'cause you're that famous.

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:50.534
-Yes.
-So, you're having a concert.

00:07:50.534 --> 00:07:52.400
You have a very public breakup.
-Yeah.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.267
-And someone, being Owen Wilson,
is in the crowd

00:07:55.267 --> 00:07:56.634
and has a sign up.

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:58.300
-Who is so good in this movie!

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.934
Oh, my God, you will love him
in this movie.

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:01.968
-He knows how to do it, right?
He knows how to do it.

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:03.501
-He just grounds
the whole thing.

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:04.901
He's just so amazing.

00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:07.234
He just has
so much heart and soul.

00:08:07.234 --> 00:08:08.567
We're so different.

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:10.667
And we're supposed to be.
We're supposed to be.

00:08:10.667 --> 00:08:11.968
-Opposites attract.
-Yes, yes.

00:08:11.968 --> 00:08:13.400
-Well, basically,
you're just fed up,

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:16.601
and someone's holding a sign up
at a concert, like you do.

00:08:16.601 --> 00:08:18.734
And his says, "Marry me,"
and you go, "Okay."

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.434
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.434 --> 00:08:22.567
-It's like, wait,
what just happened?

00:08:22.567 --> 00:08:24.367
-Nothing else is working out.

00:08:24.367 --> 00:08:26.234
How about this?
-"Okay, I'm gonna marry you."

00:08:26.234 --> 00:08:27.701
-Let's do it.
-"You want to get married?

00:08:27.701 --> 00:08:29.501
Let's just do it."
And he's like, "What?"

00:08:29.501 --> 00:08:33.033
-Yeah, and it turns into
a whole frenzy with social media

00:08:33.033 --> 00:08:35.200
and everything that happens,
and it gets out.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.601
-It's a great idea.
-Yeah. It's fun.

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:39.334
-Do you have any memorable signs

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:41.934
that you see
when you have your concerts?

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:43.200
-So many.
-Yeah.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.133
-So many.
I mean, I think when I first --

00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:46.868
I went on tour pretty late
in my career.

00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:48.300
I didn't go
until I was in my 40s

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.200
and I had kids
and everything like that.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:54.901
And so I hadn't tour for like --
I don't know how many.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.634
12 years I had been
recording music,

00:08:56.634 --> 00:08:58.667
and I had never done
a proper world tour.

00:08:58.667 --> 00:09:01.300
I'd done shows, of course,
here and there always.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.834
But I remember this woman
holding up this sign

00:09:03.834 --> 00:09:05.801
and saying, "I've been
waiting 14 years."

00:09:05.801 --> 00:09:09.100
Oh, my God,
it's gonna make me cry.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:13.601
She said -- She said,
"I've been waiting for 14 years

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:18.133
to tell you that you helped me
be the woman that I am today."

00:09:18.133 --> 00:09:20.300
I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.767
-That's cool, right?
That's powerful.

00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:25.601
Because I had never toured --
It was so sweet.

00:09:25.601 --> 00:09:27.667
It was just like
you don't realize,

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:28.901
like, your music
is touching people.

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.200
You just think you're just
doing this thing.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.367
We do this thing,
and you don't realize that

00:09:32.367 --> 00:09:35.067
until you, like, tour the world
and people come up to you,

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:36.334
and I would do
the meet and greets,

00:09:36.334 --> 00:09:38.934
and they would, you know,
tell me, like --

00:09:38.934 --> 00:09:42.133
show me tattoos of my name
on their back.

00:09:42.133 --> 00:09:44.534
And so I'm like,
"What is happening here?"

00:09:44.534 --> 00:09:46.234
And it was just amazing
to see it.

00:09:46.234 --> 00:09:47.934
So that was
a very memorable sign.

00:09:47.934 --> 00:09:49.400
I always think about that.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.934
-I'm so happy you're here.
Congrats on the film.

00:09:51.934 --> 00:09:52.901
You look great, as always.

00:09:52.901 --> 00:09:54.167
Come on.
You're always rocking it.

00:09:54.167 --> 00:09:56.701
-I'm trying to be like you, bro.
-No. Come on, buddy.

00:09:56.701 --> 00:09:59.000
Hey. Happy birthday.
Happy belated birthday.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.400
-Thank you, bro.
-Come on, buddy.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.868
If I know Maluma,
I know you probably just spent

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:06.601
a nice quiet birthday
at home, right, just chill.

00:10:06.601 --> 00:10:07.934
-It was pretty relaxed.
-Yeah.

00:10:07.934 --> 00:10:09.567
I have a video of you
at your birthday.

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:11.567
Take a look at this.
-Let me see.

00:10:11.567 --> 00:10:13.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.667 --> 00:10:16.501
-Yeah, okay.
Yeah. There you go. That's --

00:10:16.501 --> 00:10:18.634
[ Laughter ]

00:10:18.634 --> 00:10:21.200
[ Laughs ] Uh...

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.100
Last time,
we talked about your tour,

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.300
and you talked about
you're going to go

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:27.267
back to your hometown...
-Yes, sir.

00:10:27.267 --> 00:10:29.234
-...in Colombia and perform.

00:10:29.234 --> 00:10:31.167
-Yeah, have the biggest
concert of my career.

00:10:31.167 --> 00:10:33.501
It's going to be on April 30th,

00:10:33.501 --> 00:10:36.133
in the stadium in Medellín,
representing.

00:10:36.133 --> 00:10:37.467
Bro, I'm so happy.
For the first time.

00:10:37.467 --> 00:10:38.801
-Medellín.
-Yeah, for the first time,

00:10:38.801 --> 00:10:40.234
I'm going to perform
in my hometown.

00:10:40.234 --> 00:10:41.868
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-After ten years.

00:10:41.868 --> 00:10:44.133
-How does it feel?
How does it feel?

00:10:44.133 --> 00:10:45.801
-I'm nervous, to be honest.
-Yeah.

00:10:45.801 --> 00:10:48.033
-You know,
because it's not the same.

00:10:48.033 --> 00:10:50.133
Of course, I'm very blessed --
-You don't want to mess up.

00:10:50.133 --> 00:10:51.467
-Yeah, of course,
I'm very blessed

00:10:51.467 --> 00:10:53.067
that I've been touring
around the world,

00:10:53.067 --> 00:10:55.267
but nothing more important
than your hometown, bro.

00:10:55.267 --> 00:10:57.400
So, I'm going to get there,
and I have to kill it.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:58.634
-You're doing it

00:10:58.634 --> 00:11:00.200
in the country's
biggest soccer stadium.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.734
-Yes, sir.
-Which is bigger than --

00:11:01.734 --> 00:11:03.367
We can't even imagine it
really here.

00:11:03.367 --> 00:11:06.067
-Yeah, it's going to be like
45,000 people.

00:11:06.067 --> 00:11:07.200
-Wow.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.234
-So, yeah,
that's why I'm nervous.

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:09.200
-I was talking to you. I go,

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.901
"That's big. You're playing
this soccer stadium."

00:11:10.901 --> 00:11:12.767
And you go,
"Yeah, I always dreamt

00:11:12.767 --> 00:11:14.200
of being in that stadium."

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.367
I go, "Oh, that's awesome."

00:11:15.367 --> 00:11:17.601
But not as Maluma,
not as a singer.

00:11:17.601 --> 00:11:20.100
-Yeah, you're right, bro.
-You played soccer.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.767
-I wanted to be a professional
soccer player.

00:11:22.767 --> 00:11:24.601
-Can you still play?
-Yeah.

00:11:24.601 --> 00:11:26.601
-You can?
-You? You play soccer or not?

00:11:26.601 --> 00:11:30.133
-No. I get exhausted
watching soccer.

00:11:30.133 --> 00:11:31.534
-Really?
-It's exhausting.

00:11:31.534 --> 00:11:33.801
-I love playing soccer.
I still do it. I still do it.

00:11:33.801 --> 00:11:35.501
-I mean, we have a --
I have a ball here.

00:11:35.501 --> 00:11:37.467
-No way.
-Could you --

00:11:37.467 --> 00:11:40.100
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.033
-Could you show me a trick
or something?

00:11:43.033 --> 00:11:45.534
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:11:45.534 --> 00:11:46.767
-I'm feeling the pressure.

00:11:46.767 --> 00:11:48.200
-Yeah, just pretend this
is the concert.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.501
-The stadium.
-This is the stadium.

00:11:49.501 --> 00:11:50.667
Everyone's -- Yeah.

00:11:50.667 --> 00:11:52.534
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes!

00:11:52.534 --> 00:11:54.601
-Okay.

00:11:54.601 --> 00:12:01.067
♪♪

00:12:01.067 --> 00:12:02.868
-Come on, bud. Come on, man.

00:12:02.868 --> 00:12:06.801
Yeah, that's what I'm talk--
Yeah! Come on, bud!

00:12:06.801 --> 00:12:08.534
Let's go, man.

00:12:08.534 --> 00:12:11.567
What in the what?

00:12:11.567 --> 00:12:13.634
[ Laughter ]

00:12:13.634 --> 00:12:16.667
♪♪

00:12:16.667 --> 00:12:18.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:18.234 --> 00:12:19.734
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:12:19.734 --> 00:12:22.334
-Yeah, I didn't wear a cup.
I didn't wear a cup.

00:12:22.334 --> 00:12:24.167
That's Maluma right there.
Come on.

00:12:24.167 --> 00:12:25.634
You know how to do it, bud.

00:12:25.634 --> 00:12:27.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:29.934 --> 00:12:33.000
-That's why I'm singing now.
-Yeah.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.167
You just became, also,
the first recording artist

00:12:37.167 --> 00:12:39.501
to design your own bottle
for Hennessy.

00:12:39.501 --> 00:12:41.000
-Yeah.
-And this is a thing --

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.934
We're going to debut it
right now.

00:12:42.934 --> 00:12:44.734
-Yeah, bro, yeah, please.
-No one's ever seen this.

00:12:44.734 --> 00:12:47.200
-Please, please, please.
I want them to see it.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.334
I want them to see it, please.

00:12:49.334 --> 00:12:51.534
♪ Ba-da-ba-ba ♪
-♪ Da-da-da-da ♪

00:12:51.534 --> 00:12:53.267
Look at that.

00:12:53.267 --> 00:12:55.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:55.367 --> 00:12:57.601
♪♪

00:12:57.601 --> 00:13:01.567
Look at it. Look at that, bud!
-Yeah, bro.

00:13:01.567 --> 00:13:03.801
-How cool is that, man?

00:13:03.801 --> 00:13:05.167
-You like it?
-I love it!

00:13:05.167 --> 00:13:08.267
Dude, for being 28 years old
and you get to do this

00:13:08.267 --> 00:13:10.667
and play stadiums, look
at what you're doing, buddy.

00:13:10.667 --> 00:13:12.601
-Well, because
I really love Hennessy...

00:13:12.601 --> 00:13:14.767
That's why I designed it.
-Yeah. Yeah. Me too.

00:13:14.767 --> 00:13:17.601
I don't get to design
my own bottle. Yeah.

00:13:17.601 --> 00:13:18.801
This looks gorgeous, bud.

00:13:18.801 --> 00:13:20.200
-Thank you, bro.
-What goes into this?

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.634
I mean, do you look
at different things

00:13:21.634 --> 00:13:23.467
and you make a choice and
you go, "I don't like that"?

00:13:23.467 --> 00:13:25.200
-Yeah, remember
that I was doing

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.734
the "Papi Juancho" tour
here in the States.

00:13:27.734 --> 00:13:30.200
So, I was using
a lot of these colors

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:32.868
and also trying to put
my Latin culture

00:13:32.868 --> 00:13:34.667
and also
my Colombian culture.

00:13:34.667 --> 00:13:36.067
I'm from Medellín, Colombia,

00:13:36.067 --> 00:13:39.300
so I wanted just to
bring everything, what I am.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.200
And I feel proud
to be Latin, bro,

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.200
so I put everything
in this bottle.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.701
You can -- You can see it.
I feel proud, man, you know.

00:13:45.701 --> 00:13:47.501
-Good for you, buddy.
I'm proud.

00:13:47.501 --> 00:13:49.534
-Thank you, man.
-I'm proud of you, bud.

00:13:49.534 --> 00:13:52.601
Also, I think, you know --
Not only are we besties,

00:13:52.601 --> 00:13:54.934
but also --
-What else?

00:13:54.934 --> 00:13:57.133
-We are also co-stars
in a movie.

00:13:57.133 --> 00:13:58.300
-Of course, bro.

00:13:58.300 --> 00:14:00.767
-I make a cameo
in the movie "Marry Me."

00:14:00.767 --> 00:14:02.968
-Yes, sir.
And you killed it.

00:14:02.968 --> 00:14:04.067
-Yeah.
-I remember.

00:14:04.067 --> 00:14:05.667
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
It was hard for you, no?

00:14:05.667 --> 00:14:06.801
-It was really tough.

00:14:06.801 --> 00:14:08.968
I played myself.
I played myself.

00:14:08.968 --> 00:14:11.467
I was like, "Oh, what am I going
to be like in this movie?"

00:14:11.467 --> 00:14:14.234
But look at you, though.
You do a voice in "Encanto,"

00:14:14.234 --> 00:14:15.767
the biggest movie
in the world right now.

00:14:15.767 --> 00:14:18.033
-Yeah.

00:14:18.033 --> 00:14:21.434
-Crushing right now.
-Yeah, bro.

00:14:21.434 --> 00:14:24.334
That movie is nice because
they're telling the true story

00:14:24.334 --> 00:14:25.801
about Colombia.

00:14:25.801 --> 00:14:28.868
Beautiful, beautiful things are
told in the movie "Encanto."

00:14:28.868 --> 00:14:30.834
Because I don't want people
to think

00:14:30.834 --> 00:14:33.934
that Colombia is Pablo Escobar
anymore and all violence.

00:14:33.934 --> 00:14:35.701
See "Encanto," man.
It's beautiful.

00:14:35.701 --> 00:14:36.968
-That's right.
It is beautiful.

00:14:36.968 --> 00:14:40.267
-So I feel great to be
part of the movie, too.

00:14:40.267 --> 00:14:41.634
You know?
-That's awesome.

00:14:41.634 --> 00:14:43.234
Let's talk about "Marry Me."

00:14:43.234 --> 00:14:45.033
Because I'm predicting,
right now,

00:14:45.033 --> 00:14:46.601
this is going to start
a new renaissance

00:14:46.601 --> 00:14:49.167
of romantic comedies, because
it's so well done, buddy.

00:14:49.167 --> 00:14:51.334
And you and Jennifer
have chemistry.

00:14:51.334 --> 00:14:53.968
I remember we were talking
when we shot the film here.

00:14:53.968 --> 00:14:55.334
We shot a scene here.

00:14:55.334 --> 00:14:58.033
And then we went to the Garden
the night before maybe?

00:14:58.033 --> 00:15:00.501
-Yeah. The night before.
And then next day we came here.

00:15:00.501 --> 00:15:01.767
Yeah, I remember.
-Yeah.

00:15:01.767 --> 00:15:04.767
And you shot a scene
from Madison Square Garden.

00:15:04.767 --> 00:15:06.534
-Yeah, man.
-How was that?

00:15:06.534 --> 00:15:09.501
-It was nice. [ Laughs ]
-Tell the truth.

00:15:09.501 --> 00:15:11.634
-No, no, no.
-Tell the truth.

00:15:11.634 --> 00:15:13.167
-The truth -- You want me
to tell the truth?

00:15:13.167 --> 00:15:16.667
Well, I had fun,
I mean, it was nice.

00:15:16.667 --> 00:15:18.267
I was performing with Jennifer.

00:15:18.267 --> 00:15:21.667
She came like a queen,
and I just wanted to hug her,

00:15:21.667 --> 00:15:23.267
but we had a teleprompter

00:15:23.267 --> 00:15:25.300
because I didn't know
the lyrics of the song.

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:26.734
Yeah, right.

00:15:26.734 --> 00:15:31.968
And then I started singing,
and I forgot the lyrics.

00:15:31.968 --> 00:15:36.701
And I saw the teleprompter,
and the teleprompter went off.

00:15:36.701 --> 00:15:38.667
[ Laughter ]

00:15:38.667 --> 00:15:41.334
So, it was -- it was here
at the Madison Square Garden,

00:15:41.334 --> 00:15:45.133
one of the most important
concerts of my career.

00:15:45.133 --> 00:15:47.367
But, yeah -- But Jennifer,
she held me, man.

00:15:47.367 --> 00:15:49.968
-She's a pro, right?
-Yeah, yeah, she got my back.

00:15:49.968 --> 00:15:52.934
So, at the end of the day,
like, no one realized

00:15:52.934 --> 00:15:54.701
that I didn't know the lyrics.

00:15:54.701 --> 00:15:56.767
-It's a beautiful song, though.
It's an awesome song.

00:15:56.767 --> 00:15:59.000
And you're actually coming back
here to perform it on Friday.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.534
-Yeah. Yeah, on Friday,
we're going to be here.

00:16:00.534 --> 00:16:01.601
-"Marry Me."

00:16:01.601 --> 00:16:03.033
-I'm going to move
to the studio.

00:16:03.033 --> 00:16:06.234
-Just live here. I'll give you
the keys to my apartment.

00:16:06.234 --> 00:16:07.467
You can just crash tonight.
Yeah.

